# Deslop player-facing copy

Authority: [deslop skill](../skills/deslop/SKILL.md). Complements [deslop-markdown.mdc](deslop-markdown.mdc) (`.md` prose).

## When to run

After you **draft or add player-facing text** — before handoff or commit:

1. Read and follow **deslop** — Phase 0 (genre/register) → Phase 1 scan → Phase 2 rewrite → Phase 3 verify loop → Phase 4 register check.
2. Apply to **changed strings** (or the full block if you rewrote most of it).
3. Brief change log when the copy was agent-authored or the user asked for a deslop pass.

## In scope

| Kind | Examples |
|------|----------|
| **UI labels & hints** | Command rail labels, `TabbedPickerRailHints`, planning prompts, modal titles, HUD status lines, shop/service copy |
| **Item / skill / enemy text** | `DisplayName`, `Description`, `textEn`, flavor lines on content under `Assets/Content/` |
| **Help & tutorial (non-VN)** | Tooltips, codex entries, exploration warnings in HUD/modals |
| **Design content specs** | Player-facing description fields in `docs/03-content/**` (not story-event dialogue) |

## Skip

| Case | Why |
|------|-----|
| `Debug.Log`, test stubs, editor menu paths (`GridDungeonEditorMenuHints`) | Not player-facing |
| Story / VN dialogue (`docs/03-content/story-events/**`, `Assets/Content/StoryEvents/**`) | [code-review-no-story-edits.mdc](code-review-no-story-edits.mdc) — deslop only when user requests story/copy polish |
| Locked input bind vocabulary | `[Z] Confirm`, `[Directional] Navigate` — segment order per `unity-global-input-hints.mdc`; trim typos only |
| Mechanical label trims (`Skill` vs `Use Skill`) | Wording alignment, not a voice pass |
| User asked to keep wording | Respect intent |
| **Review-only** on story/content | Report slop; do not rewrite unless asked |

## Register default

**In-game UI & content** — short, direct, concrete; say what the control or item **does**. Labels stay minimal; descriptions one tight sentence when possible. No puffery or “not X but Y” framing.

## Triggers

User says **deslop**, **de-slop**, `/deslop`, **remove AI tells**, or **humanize** — run on named copy, file, or selection.

## Do not

- Change gameplay meaning, numbers, or content IDs.
- Invent lore or mechanics to sound human — use `[ADD: …]` per skill.
- Run deslop on story/dialogue during review-only passes unless the user scoped copy edits.
